{
  "name": "aphriapi",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "**Cutting-Edge BNN-VAE Architecture for High-Dimensional Posterior Dynamics**: aPhi implements Bayesian neural networks (BNNs) with variational autoencoder (VAE) layers for posterior predictive inference over embedding manifolds. Core mechanisms include spike-and-slab priors for sparse state gating, Gaussian process (GP) kernel renormalization for covariance adaptation, Dirichlet process mixtures for clustering recurrent trajectories, and Hamiltonian Monte Carlo (HMC) sampling for efficient evidence lower bound (ELBO) maximization in sharded tensor spaces. Federated variational inference across attention residuals ensures robust uncertainty quantification in gradient flows.",
